8\r\n— cavalry: 355\r\n— infantry: 1089\r\n— artillery: 5."},{"id":"regiment19-6","name":"7th (Yakar) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 817 Padstonby Era during the Gasuvyurt Rebellion. 7th (Yakar) Regiment is stationed in Yakar County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 993\r\n— cavalry: 466\r\n— archers: 937\r\n— artillery: 1."},{"id":"regiment19-7","name":"8th (Hlauggardor) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 817 Padstonby Era during the Gasuvyurt Rebellion. 8th (Hlauggardor) Regiment is stationed in Hlauggardor County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— archers: 753\r\n— cavalry: 134\r\n— infantry: 561\r\n— artillery: 2."},{"id":"regiment19-8","name":"9th (Rilasadhel) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1007 Padstonby Era during the Schizex-Telkynian War. 9th (Rilasadhel) Regiment is stationed in Herilau. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— archers: 796\r\n— artillery: 2\r\n— cavalry: 90\r\n— infantry: 524."},{"id":"regiment19-9","name":"10th (Chaulrazin) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1005 Padstonby Era during the Celofemar Invasion. 10th (Chaulrazin) Regiment is stationed in V'eldlyn. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— archers: 649\r\n— cavalry: 27\r\n— artillery: 3\r\n— infantry: 305."},{"id":"regiment19-10","name":"1st Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1010 Padstonby Era during the Schizex-Telkynian War. 1st Fleet is based in Sschidurth. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— fleet: 3."},{"id":"regiment19-11","name":"2nd Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1004 Padstonby Era during the Celofemar Invasion. 2nd Fleet is based in V'eldlyn. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— fleet: 3."},{"id":"regiment19-12","name":"3rd Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1004 Padstonby Era during the Kazashan Campaign. 3rd Fleet is based in Bal-Didrynn. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— fleet: 2."},{"id":"regiment19-13","name":"4th Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1004 Padstonby Era during the Celofemar Invasion. 4th Fleet is based in Ghrontar. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— fleet: 2."},{"id":"regiment20-0","name":"1st (Rorepeak) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 849 Padstonby Era during the Direbonfian War. 1st (Rorepeak) Regiment is stationed in Rorepeak Captaincy. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 1705\r\n— archers: 1173\r\n— cavalry: 2054\r\n— artillery: 23."},{"id":"regiment20-1","name":"2nd (Ghostme) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 791 Padstonby Era during the Smot Conquest. 2nd (Ghostme) Regiment is stationed in Millspellmi. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 1759\r\n— cavalry: 563\r\n— artillery: 40\r\n— archers: 1535."},{"id":"regiment20-2","name":"3rd (Stormburnia) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 987 Padstonby Era during the Pondkep Campaign. 3rd (Stormburnia) Regiment is stationed in Stormburnia County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 889\r\n— archers: 564\r\n— cavalry: 1434\r\n— artillery: 3."},{"id":"regiment20-3","name":"4th (Brittvate) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1006 Padstonby Era during the Chean Intervention. 4th (Brittvate) Regiment is stationed in Brittvate Shire. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 1127\r\n— archers: 623\r\n— cavalry: 809\r\n— artillery: 16."},{"id":"regiment20-4","name":"5th (Brittvate) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 990 Padstonby Era during the Pondkep Campaign. 5th (Brittvate) Regiment is stationed in Brittvate. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— infantry: 845\r\n— cavalry: 349\r\n— artillery: 23\r\n— archers: 505."},{"id":"regiment20-5","name":"1st Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1005 Padstonby Era during the Chean Intervention. 1st Fleet is based in Roseborn. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1010 PE:\r\n— fleet: 4."},{"id":"marker0","name":"Westle Volcano","legend":"Dormant volcano. Height: 5184m."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Okuztedu Hot Springs","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 20°C."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Azdurkug Creek of Luck","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker3","name":"Sshauven — gold mining town","legend":"Sshauven is a mining town of 4802 people just nearby the gold mine."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Elmalye'a — silver mining town","legend":"Elmalye'a is a mining town of 937 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Rench — tin mining town","legend":"Rench is a mining town of 2404 people just nearby the tin mine."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Bayan — copper mining town","legend":"Bayan is a mining town of 12077 people just nearby the copper mine."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Heart Bridge","legend":"A stone bridge spans over the Lastshield River near Heart."},{"id":"marker8","name":"The Purple Tiger","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious marinated hare with bright brandy is served here."},{"id":"marker9","name":"The Red Hyena","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious fried rat tails with red rom is served here."},{"id":"marker10","name":"The Hungry Tavern","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious poached lamb with ice kvass is served here."},{"id":"marker11","name":"The Superior Rat","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious corned beaver with blue vodka is served here."},{"id":"marker12","name":"The Beautiful Inn","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious syrupped pottage with sweet mead is served here."},{"id":"marker13","name":"The Far Eagle","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious stewed eggs with salty sap is served here."},{"id":"marker14","name":"The Yellow Wolverine","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious stewed eggs with cold nectar is served here."},{"id":"marker15","name":"The Giant Inn","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious stewed carrot with green water is served here."},{"id":"marker16","name":"The Orange Snake","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious smoked garlic with misty vodka is served here."},{"id":"marker17","name":"The Happy Tavern","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious syrupped tomatoes with purple beer is served here."},{"id":"marker18","name":"Egzagnod Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker19","name":"Rustcairnese Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker20","name":"Khankhirgan Waterfall","legend":"An impressive waterfall has cut through the land."},{"id":"marker21","name":"Zazilbarga Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Direbonfian Campaign. \r\nDate: February 11, 1006 Padstonby Era."},{"id":"marker22","name":"Drodh Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Zraldan War. \r\nDate: February 13, 1004 Padstonby Era."},{"id":"marker23","name":"Yalte Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Yarobanan Campaign. \r\nDate: February 18, 548 Padstonby Era."},{"id":"marker24","name":"Ghiz Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Zraz War. \r\nDate: October 12, 979 Padstonby Era."},{"id":"marker25","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2141\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2141\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker26","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2448\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2448\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker27","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=25732\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=25732\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker28","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2334\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2334\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker29","name":"Dorg Monster","legend":"Tales say a relic monster of 7 m long inhabits Dorg Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker30","name":"Newleigh Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 32 m long."},{"id":"marker31","name":"Westham Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 24 m long."},{"id":"marker32","name":"Uregkhonuur Ghoul","legend":"Tales speak of a superior Ghoul who inhabits Uregkhonuur hills and eats kids whole."},{"id":"marker33","name":"Snowden Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Anor (Human) Beliefs."},{"id":"marker34","name":"Pirksurrige Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Old Aj'Snaga (Serpents) Forefathers."},{"id":"marker35","name":"Srasarge Pinery","legend":"A pinery sacred to local Old Aj'Snaga (Serpents) Forefathers."},{"id":"marker36","name":"Malalevahoru Palm Grove","legend":"A palm grove sacred to local Rake (Drakonic) Shamanism."},{"id":"marker37","name":"Agradroz Hyenas","legend":"A gang of forest brigands."},{"id":"marker38","name":"Ayayayoba Rats","legend":"A gang of forest bandits."},{"id":"marker39","name":"Kutluman Bisons","legend":"A gang of forest bandits."},{"id":"marker40","name":"Kulukk Scorpions","legend":"A gang of forest highwaymen."},{"id":"marker41","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker42","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker43","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker44","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker45","name":"Farith Column","legend":"An ancient column. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">\ud802𐠱\udc20𐠣\ud802\ud802𐠵\ud802𐠅\ud802𐠊\udc21\udc18\udc14 \udc24𐠜\udc16\udc0a\ud802\ud802\ud802𐠛\ud802𐠁\ud802\ud802𐠟\ud802𐠦\udc14\ud802𐠿\udc37\ud802\ud802𐠞\udc14\udc23\ud802\ud802𐠰𐠞\udc29\ud802𐠸𐠈\udc20 \udc10\ud802 \udc08\udc10\ud802𐠴\udc16\ud802𐠵</div>"},{"id":"marker46","name":"Zrag Column","legend":"An ancient column. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">\udc34\udc29𐠼𐠂\udc04\udc30\udc1e\udc3c𐠫\ud802\ud802𐠵\udc16\udc1a\udc14\udc1a\udc04\ud802\ud802𐠌\ud802 \udc0b𐠋\ud802\ud802𐠘\udc17\udc2b\ud802𐠟\ud802𐠠𐠓\ud802\ud802\ud802</div>"},{"id":"marker47","name":"Kophrash Pillar","legend":"An ancient pillar. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">༪༿༄༲༯༾༽༗༜༖༘༳༉༅༡༙༛༡༣༧༚༌༕༒༖༽༯༭༁༢༢༰༌༓་༑༅ༀ༶༧༬༌༉༰༶༁༖༜༺༢༌༴༿༉༄༦༶༠༂༊༕༫༬༳༛༷་༖༆༲༙༙༐༄༑༆༛༃ༀ༚༇༦༌༦</div>"},{"id":"marker48","name":"Ayburbur Sculpture","legend":"An ancient sculpture. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">\udc25\udc23\udc20𐠷\udc01\udc21\udc04\udc3f𐠖\udc0f\udc3f𐠿\udc0b\ud802  \ud802𐠍\udc15\ud802𐠄\udc1c\udc22𐠌𐠧𐠲𐠿\udc1f 𐠣\ud802\ud802</div>"},{"id":"marker49","name":"Ruined Fortification","legend":"Ruins of an ancient fortification. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker50","name":"Ruined Temple","legend":"Ruins of an ancient temple. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker51","name":"Ruined Pyramid","legend":"Ruins of an ancient pyramid. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker52","name":"Ruined City","legend":"Ruins of an ancient city. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker53","name":"Nudhnugh Collection","legend":"A vast collection of knowledge, including many rare and ancient tomes."},{"id":"marker54","name":"Travelling Wondrous Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this wondrous circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker55","name":"Travelling Breathtaking Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this breathtaking circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker56","name":"Zuzecceg Tournament","legend":"Warriors from around the land gather for a tournament of might in Zuzecceg, with fame, fortune and favour on offer to the victor."},{"id":"marker57","name":"Boulport Fair","legend":"A fair is being held in Boulport, with all manner of local and foreign goods and services on offer."},{"id":"marker58","name":"Minor Jetty","legend":"A small location along the Dograme River to launch boats from sits here, along with a weary looking owner, willing to sell passage along the river."},{"id":"marker59","name":"Larks migration","legend":"A huge group of larks are migrating, whether part of their annual routine, or something more extraordinary."},{"id":"marker60","name":"Suntas ball","legend":"A ball has been organised at Suntas as a chance to gather the local elders of the area together to be merry, make alliances and scheme around the crisis."},{"id":"marker61","name":"Peculiar mirage","legend":"This peculiar mirage has been luring travellers out of their way for eons."},{"id":"marker62","name":"Bres Hole","legend":"The Bres Hole. Locals claim that it is totally empty."},{"id":"marker63","name":"Curgarde Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker64","name":"Cen'kas Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker65","name":"Passej'tir Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker66","name":"Cragle Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker67","name":"Schizex Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker68","name":"Velgmukh Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker69","name":"Kesen Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker70","name":"Shroudrock Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker71","name":"Nird Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker72","name":"Brukh Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker73","name":"Birakinb Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but